torney general shall investigate violations of the law of this state respecting unfair, discriminatory, and other unlawful practices in business, commerce, or trade, and specifically, but not exclusively … the Prevention of Consumer Fraud Act (sections 325F.68 to 325F.70)","line":26,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-2-1-1-474c0b89","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":8,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"2","text":"Minn. Stat. §§ 8.31, 8.32, 299C.061, subd. 4(c)","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"MN-Stat-ch-8","target_page":"10","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 8.32, subd. 2(1)","status":"verified","target_quote":"The attorney general shall: (1) enforce the provisions of law relating to consumer fraud and unlawful practices in connection therewith as set forth in sections 325F.68 and 325F.69","line":27,"k":2,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-2-1-2-474c0b89","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":10,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"2","text":"Minn. Stat. §§ 8.31, 8.32, 299C.061, subd. 4(c)","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"MN-Stat-299C.061","target_page":"2","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 299C.061, subd. 4(c)","status":"verified","target_quote":"Notwithstanding paragraph (b), this section has no effect on the authority of the attorney general to investigate and enforce violations or suspected violations of Minnesota civil or criminal law.","line":28,"k":3,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-2-1-3-474c0b89","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"2","text":"ECF No. 11 at 8","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-011","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 8","status":"verified","target_quote":"does not disavow the AGO's jurisdiction to investigate violations of PCFA, only the ability to investigate and prosecute criminal matters … the AGO does investigate and prosecute Medicaid fraud","line":29,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-2-1-1-e28b8ffa","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"2","text":"ECF No. 16 at 5","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-016","target_page":"5","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 5","status":"verified","target_quote":"simply states that the Attorney General must investigate violations of the PCFA and has the discretion to","line":30,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-2-1-1-754e876d","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"3","text":"County of Mille Lacs v. Benjamin, 361 F.3d 460, 464–65","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2004 - County of Mille Lacs v. Benjamin, 361 F.3d 460 (8th Cir.) [CA8 slip No. 03-2527, 9 Mar. 2004]","target_page":"7","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"464–65","status":"verified","target_quote":"district court is generally barred from dismissing a case with prejudice if it concludes subject matter jurisdiction is absent","line":31,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-029-3-1-1-c345040d","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-029","src_page":"3","text":"Dalton v. NPC Int'l, Inc., 932 F.3d 693, 696","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2019 - Dalton v. NPC International, Inc., 932 F.3d 693 (8th Cir.) [C